<!--
  Data extraction rules for Android 12+ (API 31+).

  Referenced from AndroidManifest.xml via android:dataExtractionRules.

  twoyi ships an entire Android image (rootfs + system + userdata) inside
  its private data dir, plus any user-installed APKs and per-profile
  state. A device-to-device migration or a cloud backup that pulled this
  tree to another phone would (a) leak every file the user installed
  inside the VM, and (b) almost certainly fail to boot on the target
  because the native libraries are ABI-specific and the data layout is
  tied to the source install path. We therefore opt out of *both* the
  cloud-backup path and the device-transfer path.

  allowBackup="false" in the manifest already disables Auto Backup on
  Android 6–11; this file covers the Android 12+ migration flow, which
  has its own separate flag and would otherwise still run.

  The include-then-exclude pattern on domain="root" is the documented
  way to express "exclude everything" — Android requires at least one
  <include> rule per domain before <exclude> is meaningful, and an
  empty <cloud-backup/> / <device-transfer/> element is treated as
  "no rules" rather than "exclude everything".
-->
<data-extraction-rules>
    <cloud-backup>
        <include domain="root" />
        <exclude domain="root" />
    </cloud-backup>
    <device-transfer>
        <include domain="root" />
        <exclude domain="root" />
    </device-transfer>
</data-extraction-rules>
